Bunnie Xo Is Having a &#8216;Baddie Bunnie Summer&#8217; After Jelly Roll Divorce: &#8216;I&#8217;m Just&nbsp;Thriving&#8217;

Bunnie Xo Says She&#8217;ll &#8216;Never&#8217; Get Married Again After Jelly Roll Split, Recalls &#8216;Betrayal Trauma&#8217; of His&nbsp;Affair

Bunnie Xo Reacts to Jelly Roll&#8217;s Daughter Claiming Internet Would &#8216;Crumble&#8217; If Full Truth of Their Divorce Came&nbsp;Out

In the full interview posted Thursday (Sept. 3), the podcaster began by acknowledging how some people have assumed that she isn&#8217;t sad about the divorce due to the strong face she&#8217;s put on publicly since her marriage ended. &#8220;I think that&#8217;s why everybody is mistaken, because I&#8217;m not crying on my phone on social media,&#8221; she said. &#8220;My heart was shattered, but guess what? It&#8217;s healing, and it&#8217;s coming back even stronger.&#8221;

&#8220;There [were] moments when my team had to pick me up off the floor and give me IVs,” Bunnie continued. “I wasn’t eating. I was eating baby food to get by. I lost 20 pounds. Heartbreak, man. It’s the best freaking diet.&#8221;

She added, &#8220;I don’t want people to think like I’m just out here acting like s&#8211;t doesn’t hurt … Yeah, it hurt.&#8221;

The Dumb Blonde host also shared what she sees for herself and her career now that she&#8217;s flying solo. &#8220;I always kind of water myself down [in romantic relationships], and I always am trying to put them first,&#8221; she told Hager. &#8220;Even though I have been majorly successful on my own, it&#8217;s still not fully me &#8230; I&#8217;m kind of stepping into my own spotlight now, and I don&#8217;t have anyone else around me. It&#8217;s just me holding the show, the attention.&#8221;

Jelly filed to divorce Bunnie after nearly 10 years of marriage in May, news that only became public in June. Shortly afterward, Bunnie posted a since-deleted podcast episode explaining that the split stemmed from a heated argument that took place on Mother&#8217;s Day this year, during which she dared the country star to file divorce papers without thinking that he actually would.

&#8220;Was I blindsided? Was this divorce mutual? No, it was not mutual, even though I told him to file the divorce papers, I was speaking out of anger and just frustration,&#8221; she said on Dumb Blonde , revealing that she and Jelly remain &#8220;best friends&#8221; and still plan on welcoming a baby via IVF together. &#8220;But was it necessary for us to have a wakeup call? … Absolutely. … My husband and I are ending this marriage on the best possible terms that you could ever have a divorce.”

